#!/usr/bin/python3
"""tangerine-gate: form login, sessions and an audit log for nginx auth_request.

nginx asks GET /_gate/check on every request; we answer 204 (+ X-Tangerine-User)
or 401. Login, logout and the admin page live under /_gate/.

Who may log in comes from the `users:` section of config.yaml; password hashes
live separately in the passwords file, managed with `tangerine-gate passwd`.
Both files are re-read automatically when they change.

Needs PyYAML; python3-maxminddb is used for IP geolocation when installed.

    tangerine-gate serve
    tangerine-gate passwd NAME [--random | --delete]
    tangerine-gate users
    tangerine-gate log [-n N] [--user NAME] [--failed]
    tangerine-gate sessions
    tangerine-gate revoke (SID | --user NAME)
"""
